Notebook[{Cell["DecomposeRepresentation", "ObjectName"], 
  Cell["DecomposeRepresentation[g, r] decomposes the representation r of the \
group or context g into irreducible blocks, returning the block Rep, the \
multiplicities and a verified embedding U with M.U == U.block for every \
generator matrix M.", "Usage"], Cell["Status: Alpha.", "Notes"], 
  Cell["DecomposeRepresentation[g, r] validates r, computes its \
multiplicities and returns Rep (the block representation built from the \
target irreps, unchanged), Blocks (CharacterID, Copy, Indices, Target), \
Multiplicities, Embedding U with M.U == U.block for every generator matrix M, \
BasisChange (Inverse[U]), InverseBasisChange (U), Arithmetic and Validation."\
, "Notes"], Cell["Targets are the group's stored irreps (computed on a live \
group when missing) or TargetRepresentations, an association irrep ID -> Rep \
covering every constituent and validated against its irrep. Basis -> \
\"Unitary\" (default) uses unitary targets and orthonormal multiplicity \
coordinates: U^\[Dagger].H.U == I for an invariant form H of r, so U is \
unitary when r is. Basis -> \"General\" accepts general targets.", "Notes"], 
  Cell["Method -> Automatic tries, for exact cyclotomic input on a live group \
(or a context whose group is live in this kernel), the native GAP routes \
\"Serre\", \"Alternative\" and \"Canonical\" (RepnDecomp, with the targets \
supplied as irreps), \"REPSNConstituents\" and \"REPSNBlocks\", then \
\"GeneratorEquations\", which solves M.X == X.D for each constituent in \
Wolfram exactly (or numerically with Arithmetic -> \"Numerical\"). A native \
route supplies intertwiner bases checked in GAP; normalization and the exact \
proofs are the same for every route. IsomorphismMethod selects the native \
alignment. Validation reports the Method used and the Attempts.", "Notes"], 
  Cell["UnitarizationMethod chooses the invariant form of the unitary \
coordinates (recorded under Validation \"UnitarizationMethod\"); FieldMethod \
chooses the exact domain (Validation \"Domain\").", "Notes"], 
  Cell["Options (shared configured settings can override these defaults):", 
   "Notes"], Cell[BoxData[GridBox[{{Cell[" ", "TableRowIcon"], 
       Cell[BoxData["GroupModel"], "TableText"], Cell["Automatic", 
        "TableText"], Cell["Automatic, \"Original\", \"Permutation\" or \
\"PC\" for new method calculations; PC requires a solvable group. Restoration \
and compatible cache hits do not convert models. Import uses it only when \
computing a new character-validation source.", "TableText"]}, 
      {Cell[" ", "TableRowIcon"], Cell[BoxData["StoreGAPState"], 
        "TableText"], Cell["True", "TableText"], Cell["True retains verified \
state across calls; False keeps only call-local temporary checkpoints. Cached \
mathematical values remain available.", "TableText"]}, 
      {Cell[" ", "TableRowIcon"], Cell[BoxData["AttemptTimeLimit"], 
        "TableText"], Cell["600", "TableText"], Cell["Positive seconds or \
Infinity, per attempt including verification and saving. Automatic method \
attempts each receive this limit.", "TableText"]}, 
      {Cell[" ", "TableRowIcon"], Cell[BoxData["CoreBudget"], "TableText"], 
       Cell["Automatic", "TableText"], Cell["Positive integer at most \
$ProcessorCount, or Automatic to use the available count. Sequential \
algorithms run as separate worker processes.", "TableText"]}, 
      {Cell[" ", "TableRowIcon"], Cell[BoxData["MemoryBudget"], "TableText"], 
       Cell["Automatic", "TableText"], Cell["Positive integer bytes, or \
Automatic using half system memory less current kernel usage. Admission \
estimates and sampled total worker RSS enforce the allocation.", 
        "TableText"]}, {Cell[" ", "TableRowIcon"], 
       Cell[BoxData["ProgressFunction"], "TableText"], 
       Cell["Automatic", "TableText"], Cell["Automatic shows a notebook \
monitor when a front end is available; None is silent; a Function or user \
symbol receives progress associations. Callbacks should return promptly; \
failures/cancellation clean owned workers.", "TableText"]}, 
      {Cell[" ", "TableRowIcon"], Cell[BoxData["FieldMethod"], "TableText"], 
       Cell["Automatic", "TableText"], Cell["Automatic, \"Cyclotomic\", \
\"PrimitiveElement\", \"Radical\", \"RootReduce\" or a duplicate-free list of \
these.", "TableText"]}, {Cell[" ", "TableRowIcon"], 
       Cell[BoxData["UnitarizationMethod"], "TableText"], 
       Cell["Automatic", "TableText"], Cell["\"GroupAverage\" averages \
M^\[Dagger].M over the image of the group; \"GeneratorEquations\" solves \
M^\[Dagger].H.M == H on the generators and chooses a positive solution; \
\"BSGSAverage\" is a native GAP route (automatic representation computation \
and TransformGroupRepresentations in GAP) and is refused where the work runs \
in Wolfram.", "TableText"]}, {Cell[" ", "TableRowIcon"], 
       Cell[BoxData["Method"], "TableText"], Cell["Automatic", "TableText"], 
       Cell["See the method choices in this page's details.", "TableText"]}, 
      {Cell[" ", "TableRowIcon"], Cell[BoxData["IsomorphismMethod"], 
        "TableText"], Cell["Automatic", "TableText"], 
       Cell["Selects the native alignment of decomposition subspaces to the \
target irreps: \"BSGS\" (RepnDecomp's stabilizer-chain group sum), \
\"GroupAverage\" (a sum over the group) and \"OrbitSum\" apply to one copy of \
a target on an irreducible subspace; \"GeneratorEquations\" solves the \
intertwiner equations for any multiplicity. Automatic tries them in that \
order where they apply. A native IsomorphismMethod with Method -> \
\"GeneratorEquations\" or numerical arithmetic is refused.", "TableText"]}, 
      {Cell[" ", "TableRowIcon"], Cell[BoxData["TargetRepresentations"], 
        "TableText"], Cell["Automatic", "TableText"], 
       Cell["Automatic uses the group's stored active irreps in the requested \
basis, computing missing ones on a live group; an association irrep ID -> Rep \
supplies the targets, each validated against the same group and its irrep ID, \
and must cover every constituent.", "TableText"]}, 
      {Cell[" ", "TableRowIcon"], Cell[BoxData["Basis"], "TableText"], 
       Cell["\"Unitary\"", "TableText"], Cell["\"Unitary\" requires unitary \
matrices on every recorded generator; \"General\" accepts any verified basis. \
\"UnitaryTDiagonal\" (ComputeGroupRepresentations, the builders and \
TransformGroupRepresentations) additionally requires the assigned T to be \
diagonal, with its phases in the TPhaseOrder order and the PhaseConvention \
applied (the group needs a modular S,T assignment). SetGroupRepresentation \
and ChangeGroupRepBasis accept \"Unitary\" and \"General\"; \
TransformGroupRepresentations \"Unitary\" and \"UnitaryTDiagonal\". For \
DiagonalizeRepresentationT, \"Unitary\" requires unitary input and keeps the \
result unitary.", "TableText"]}, {Cell[" ", "TableRowIcon"], 
       Cell[BoxData["Arithmetic"], "TableText"], Cell["\"Exact\"", 
        "TableText"], Cell["\"Exact\" proves identities exactly and refuses \
numerical input; \"Numerical\" works at WorkingPrecision (default 50) and \
checks residuals against Tolerance (default 10^(-Floor[p/2])). Tolerance is \
accepted only with numerical arithmetic.", "TableText"]}, 
      {Cell[" ", "TableRowIcon"], Cell[BoxData["WorkingPrecision"], 
        "TableText"], Cell["50", "TableText"], 
       Cell["See the method choices in this page's details.", "TableText"]}, 
      {Cell[" ", "TableRowIcon"], Cell[BoxData["Tolerance"], "TableText"], 
       Cell["Automatic", "TableText"], 
       Cell["See the method choices in this page's details.", "TableText"]}, 
      {Cell[" ", "TableRowIcon"], Cell[BoxData["Verification"], "TableText"], 
       Cell["Automatic", "TableText"], Cell["Automatic, \"Exact\", \
\"Numerical\" or None (the Validate functions: Automatic, \"Exact\" or \
\"Numerical\"; the modular-form functions have no \"Exact\" route).", 
        "TableText"]}}, GridBoxAlignment -> {"Columns" -> {{Left}}}, 
     GridBoxItemSize -> {"Columns" -> {Scaled[0.02], Scaled[0.3], 
         Scaled[0.18], Scaled[0.5]}}]], "3ColumnTableMod"], 
  Cell["See Also", "SeeAlsoSection"], 
  Cell[TextData[{ButtonBox["ValidateRepresentation", 
      BaseStyle -> "Hyperlink", ButtonData -> {"ValidateRepresentation.nb", 
        None}], "  |  ", ButtonBox["TargetRepresentations", 
      BaseStyle -> "Hyperlink", ButtonData -> {"TargetRepresentations.nb", 
        None}], "  |  ", ButtonBox["IsomorphismMethod", 
      BaseStyle -> "Hyperlink", ButtonData -> {"IsomorphismMethod.nb", 
        None}], "  |  ", ButtonBox["ComputeGroupRepresentations", 
